From 1b8f05e61fc217ba131223768556e9a59a560fa2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ereaxff-build <build@localhost>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 02:02:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/9] Add classical_atoms option to <dynamics>: classical
 particles inside path-integral runs

A classical atom keeps the internal normal modes of its ring polymer at zero
(q_k = p_k = 0, k >= 1). In i-PI's convention this gives the physical mass,
the bead-averaged force and temperature T. Thermostat noise that is removed
is booked in ensemble.eens; momentum removed after a force kick is not.

Also: temperature property corrected for projected modes; kinetic_td refuses
classical atoms; coupled_harmonic test PES; statistical and conservation tests.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
